# Git hygiene

## On commit

- Run `git status` + `git diff --cached` (or full diff of what will be committed).
- Reject/warn on filenames and content: `.env*`, `credentials`, `service_account`, `*.pem`, `*.key`, `id_rsa`, `Authorization: Bearer`, `AKIA…`, `BEGIN … PRIVATE KEY`, long base64-looking secrets in source.
- If unsure, ask before committing.
- Never use `--no-verify` unless the user explicitly requests it.

## On push

- Never push commits meant for `main` / `master` / `deploy/dev` by committing on those branches — use a feature branch + PR (see `pr-workflow`).
- Invoke **review-before-push**: summarize commits, target branch, whether merge would trigger deploy (`deploy/dev` → Oracle via GHA), confirm no secrets in `@{upstream}..HEAD` (or equivalent), and cite full `pytest` green.
- Do not push until the user confirms, unless they already ordered push/deploy in the same turn.
